  "knowledge": "PostgreSQL answers COMMIT with the command tag COMMIT, so the client knows that the transaction committed.",
  "api_outcome": {
    "reported": "committed",
    "basis": "Session.begin() exited without an exception, so it committed",
    "contract": "Session.begin() as a context manager commits when the block exits without an exception and rolls back when the block exits with one. Session.begin_nested() is a SAVEPOINT; an exception there rolls back to the savepoint, and a failure of that rollback propagates. If commit() raises on the way out, TransactionalContext.__exit__ calls rollback() when it can and propagates the error from that exit.",
